# Paths umbral-lint skips in THIS repo.
#
# A style guide has to quote the things it forbids. These paths exist to document
# violations, so linting them reports the documentation rather than any real defect.
# Everything else in the repo IS linted — see `npm run lint`.

# The audit records what the live products actually rendered, including the v1.0
# token values and the Google Fonts links it was written to expose.
audit/

# Superseded v1.0 material, kept for reference only.
_inbox/

# The linter's own patterns are, necessarily, the strings it looks for.
tools/umbral-lint/

# The build inputs: the token sources are where values are supposed to live, and
# the generators embed example output.
tokens/src/
build/

# The plan and the agent contract, both of which quote counter-examples.
kickoff-prompt.md
CLAUDE.md

# The `dont:` field of every rule is a counter-example by definition, and three
# generated artifacts inherit it verbatim.
rules/rules.yaml
guide/_includes/
skills/umbral-brand/references/

# lint.py necessarily contains the strings it detects; the other two scripts are linted.
skills/umbral-brand/scripts/lint.py
